sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The vertebrate face is patterned by bioelectric gradients that regionalize gene expression, and reproducing these voltage patterns elsewhere in a tadpole by misexpressing specific ion channels induces whole ectopic organs such as eyes on the gut or tail, regions not otherwise competent to make eyes in response to Pax6.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reproducing face bioelectric patterns via ion-channel misexpression induces ectopic eyes";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “Bioelectric control: a mechanism for scaling cell behaviors to large-scale morphogenetic goals”. Scope: Xenopus laevis embryos and tadpoles"
}
